# Development and delivery

**Prerequisites:** [compilation model](/docs/concepts/compilation-model/).
**Kind:** concept.
**Next:** [Package and deploy](/docs/how-to/package-and-deploy/).

| Mode | What runs |
| --- | --- |
| `rocci view` / `browse` | Lower, compile, preview one component or gallery |
| `rocci run` | Generated or custom server plus optional preview window |
| `rocci build --release` | Linux server tree + `assets/` |
| `rocci bundle` | Ad-hoc macOS `.app` around the same HTTP server |

Rocci invokes the Roc toolchain. It does not embed Roc's interpreter.
Interpreter-backed preview is a design opportunity, not a shipped feature.

The preview window and a normal browser share the loopback origin. Production
is the release server (or the `.app` wrapping it), not the Dev panel.

**Related:** [Ship](/docs/tutorials/ship/), [Status](/docs/status/).
